https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

Everything under this directory is a Derivative Database of OpenStreetMap.

  (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database License.
  https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

The contents are cut from an OpenStreetMap planet file, which is distributed
under ODbL:

  https://planet.openstreetmap.org/pbf/planet-260831.osm.pbf
  94,612,383,571 bytes, md5 c67437924cf55de40e8708c7192f354d

That snapshot of 2026-08-31 is the only source. The
extract covers the 23 special wards of Tokyo and nothing else. The boundary
used to cut it is itself taken from that same snapshot, so the geometry in
tokyo23_osm_boundary.geojson is OSM data too and carries ODbL.

The Parquet files under parquet/ are the same records loaded into PostGIS with
osm2pgsql and written back out. They are a reformatting, not new data, and
carry ODbL unchanged. So does anything built from them: a database you load
them into, an index, a set of question and answer pairs whose answers are
computed from them.

provenance.yaml records the versions of every tool in the chain, because the
column layout of the Parquet files is decided by osm2pgsql's style file rather
than by anything in this repository.

ODbL-1.0 section 4.2 permits redistribution to satisfy the notice requirement
by including either a copy of the licence or its URI. This file supplies the
URI above. The full text is at that address.

The MIT licence in the source repository covers the code that builds this and
does not apply here.
